Habitat types</li>\n                                <li>• Adaptations</li>\n                                <li>• Biodiversity</li>\n                                <li>• Conservation</li>\n                            </ul>\n                        </a>\n                    </div>\n                </section>\n\n                <!-- Learning Path -->\n                <section>\n                    <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4\">Learning Path</h2>\n                    <div class=\"bg-white/50 rounded-lg p-6\">\n                        <ol class=\"space-y-4 text-gray-700\">\n                            <li class=\"flex items-start\">\n                                <span class=\"font-medium mr-2\">1.</span>\n                                <div>\n                                    <p class=\"font-medium\">Begin with Ecological Concepts</p>\n                                    <p class=\"text-sm text-gray-600 mt-1\">Master the fundamental principles and relationships in ecology.</p>\n                                </div>\n                            </li>\n                            <li class=\"flex items-start\">\n                                <span class=\"font-medium mr-2\">2.</span>\n                                <div>\n                                    <p class=\"font-medium\">Study Ecosystem Function</p>\n                                    <p class=\"text-sm text-gray-600 mt-1\">Understand how energy and materials flow through ecosystems.</p>\n                                </div>\n                            </li>\n                            <li class=\"flex items-start\">\n                                <span class=\"font-medium mr-2\">3.</span>\n                                <div>\n                                    <p class=\"font-medium\">Explore Population Ecology</p>\n                                    <p class=\"text-sm text-gray-600 mt-1\">Learn how populations grow, interact, and change over time.</p>\n          